import json
R = json.load(open("results.json")); T = json.load(open("tour_ref.json"))
def pc(x, d=1): return f"{100*x:.{d}f}%"
def am(dec):
    return f"+{round((dec-1)*100)}" if dec >= 2 else f"-{round(100/(dec-1))}"
L = []
a = L.append
a("# ATP Shanghai Masters 1000 - Sunday Oct 11, 2026 - model report")
a("")
a("Generated 2026-10-11 ~13:35 UTC. Re-runnable: `sim.py`, `calib_sigma.py`, `run_atp.py`, `tour_ref.py`, `gen_report.py` in this folder (`results.json`, `tour_ref.json` are the outputs). No sportsbook/app was logged into or scraped; only public search snippets (page fetches are blocked by the proxy, so every number below comes from a search snippet or from the model).")
a("")
a("## 0. Read this first (timing and data-quality flags)")
a("")
a("1. **Timing problem.** Shanghai is UTC+8. The Oct 11 (China-date) sessions are listed by P1 Travel as a day session at 12:30 and an evening session at 18:30 local = **04:30 UTC and 10:30 UTC** ([P1 Travel](https://www.p1travel.com/fr/tennis/atp-world-tours/atp-shanghai-masters-11-october-day-session)). At 13:00 UTC it is already 21:00 in Shanghai, so most or all of the Oct 11 China-date matches below are probably **finished or in their last match**. Exact per-match start times were **not found** (Bleacher Nation lists 'TBA'). Aggregators also disagree on dates: wincomparator and ats.io label these matches 11/10/2026, Kalshi shows De Minaur-Sakamoto at 'Sunday Oct 11, 12:00am EDT' (= 04:00 UTC), and a ran.de preview lists Zverev-Halys as 'Sunday 11 / Monday 12 October, ca. 6:30' ([ran.de](https://ran.joyn.de/sports/tennis/atp/alexander-zverev-im-sechzehntelfinale-von-shanghai-hier-laeuft-das-match-gegen-quentin-halys-live-im-tv-stream-ticker-198739)). So some of these could still be on the China-date Oct 12 card (starting 04:30 UTC Oct 12 = 11:30 PM US Central tonight). **Treat every price below as a stale pre-match snapshot and re-check the live order of play before betting anything.**")
a("2. **No other ATP-level event today.** The next ATP events are Almaty (Oct 19-25) and Brussels/Lyon (Oct 19-25), then Basel/Vienna, Stockholm Nov 8-14 ([Too Many Rackets](https://toomanyrackets.com/2026-atp-tournament-schedule/), [Sports Digest](https://sportsdigest.in/2026-atp-tour-calendar-list-events/171916/amp/)). Sinner withdrew from Shanghai ([EWN](https://www.ewn.co.za/2026/10/03/world-no1-sinner-pulls-out-of-shanghai-masters-to-delay-return)); Djokovic lost to Hurkacz 6-4 6-3 on Oct 9 ([KSL](https://www.ksl.com/article/51634429/tennis-hurkacz-dumps-djokovic-out-of-shanghai-masters-to-reach-third-round)).")
a("3. **Serve/return stats were NOT found in snippets** for these players (no tennis-abstract/ATP serve pages reachable). The hold%/break% profiles I feed the simulator are **my assumptions from general knowledge** (labelled below). They only shape tiebreak/3-set structure and one of the inputs to `p_model`; win probabilities are anchored to market + third-party model numbers.")
a("4. **Odds source is thin.** Moneyline decimals come from wincomparator's preview pages (book unspecified, ~5% two-way overround); Kalshi gave one cross-check. bet365's real prices were not accessible. Totals lines were found for only 3 of 7 matches.")
a("5. **No outcome data was reachable**, so the model cannot be backtested for Brier/log-loss. Validation below is internal-consistency only.")
a("")
a("## 1. Slate (all hard court, outdoor, Qizhong Forest Sports City Arena; Round of 32 = 'third round' in the 96-draw)")
a("")
a("Source for the 5-match list: [Bleacher Nation schedule](https://www.bleachernation.com/how-to-watch/2026/10/09/rolex-shanghai-masters-schedule-sunday-october-11-matchups-tv-live-stream-info/); Khachanov-Mannarino and Hurkacz-Zhou from [wincomparator](https://www.wincomparator.com/predictions/karen-khachanov-adrian-mannarino-8884860/) / [wincomparator](https://www.wincomparator.com/predictions/hurkacz-h-pol-yi-miao-zhou-8884945/). There may be an 8th match I could not find.")
a("")
a("| Match | Round | Time (UTC) | ML decimal (fav / dog) | American | No-vig fav | Total-games line found |")
a("|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
for r in R:
    tl = f"{r['total_line']} ({r['total_src']})" if r["total_line"] else r["total_src"]
    a(f"| {r['A']} v {r['B']} | R32 | TBD (sessions ~04:30 / ~10:30) | {r['decA']:.2f} / {r['decB']:.2f} | {am(r['decA'])} / {am(r['decB'])} | {pc(r['p_mkt'])} | {tl} |")
a("")
a("Market notes: De Minaur-Sakamoto no-vig is the average of Kalshi's 68% ([Kalshi](https://kalshi.com/markets/kxatpmatch/atp-tennis-match/kxatpmatch-26oct09desak)) and wincomparator's 1.29/3.75 (74.4%). Tiafoe-Davidovich Fokina: only Tiafoe's 1.73 was found; DF's price is **ASSUMED** from a 4.5% overround (2.14). Mensik is the market favourite (1.62 vs Cerundolo 2.30) even though wincomparator's own model picks Cerundolo (56.3%), Cerundolo leads the head-to-head (2-0 / 3-0 by source) and beat him 6-3 6-3 last week in Beijing ([Sportytrader](https://www.sportytrader.com/us/picks/francisco-cerundolo-jakub-mensik-378060/)). Shelton-Gea: wincomparator's odds (1.36 / 3.20) look short for a rank-8 vs rank-82 match (Elo-based ~82-85%) so the book price may be stale or soft.")
a("")
a("## 2. Method")
a("")
a("- **Point model:** each player has an iid probability of winning a point on serve; games use the exact hold formula, tiebreaks are simulated point-by-point (1-2-2-2 serve pattern), three sets with a final-set tiebreak (Masters rule), correct serve-order carry-over. 400,000 simulated matches per fixture.")
a(f"- **Day-form noise:** each player draws a persistent per-match shift ~N(0, sigma) in point-win probability (+ for his serve, - for his opponent's). sigma = 0.0205 was chosen so a tour-like mix of favourites (fav win prob 52-88%, 80.5% average hold) gives a **{pc(T['mix']['p3'])} three-set rate** (target 38%; the same mix gives mean {T['mix']['mean']:.1f} total games). Sensitivity run: sigma = 0.027 (about 35-36% three-set rate, matching Tennis Abstract's tour figure).")
a("- **Assumed profiles (not sourced):** hold% / break% on hard - " + "; ".join(f"{r['A']} {int(r['holdA']*100)}/{int(r['brkA']*100)}, {r['B']} {int(r['holdB']*100)}/{int(r['brkB']*100)}" for r in R) + ". Tour average assumed 80.5% hold. Sakamoto's high hold reflects 10.6 aces/match and 91.9% tournament hold in snippets ([Dimers](https://www.dimers.com/tennis/news/rei-sakamoto-vs-andrey-rublev-tennis-prediction-atp-shanghai-masters-2026-ac), [MediaPronos](https://mediapronos.com/?p=679855)).")
a("- **Benter blend:** `p_blend = 0.3*p_model + 0.7*p_market_novig`. `p_model` = mean of (third-party model probabilities found, plus the assumed-profile simulator win probability `p_stats`). Edge = `p_blend * decimal - 1`; stake = quarter-Kelly of `edge/(decimal-1)`. The simulator is then re-calibrated so each match's win probability equals `p_blend` before totals are read off.")
a("- **Totals:** market line treated as a 50/50 market, so `p_blend(over) = 0.3*P_model(over) + 0.35`; assumed -110 both sides (break-even 52.4%). Pick'em thresholds: 2-pick 57.7% -> raw model p >= 75.7%; 3-pick 55.0% -> p >= 66.7%; 4-pick 56.2%; 5-pick 54.9%.")
a("")
a("## 3. Win probabilities, Benter blend and moneyline edges")
a("")
a("| Fav v Dog | p_stats (assumed profiles) | third-party models | p_model | p_market (no-vig) | **p_blend fav** | Fav edge | Dog edge | Dog break-even price for 0% edge |")
a("|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
